{"t": 1794124755.7402575, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Production reconciliation regression traced to this change: [LEDGER-WORKER-9A](https://us.sentry.io/organizations/acme/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/) reports ReconciliationMismatch (expected 1100, got 1099), first seen in ledger-worker@2026.11.3, and identifies commit 8c2f1d0. The commit diff changes `round(amount_minor * rate)` to `int(amount_minor * rate)` in worker/rates.py, truncating instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit.\n\nFix prepared locally: restore `return round(amount_minor * rate)`. Added regression coverage for rounding up/down, negative amounts, zero, and the previous ties-to-even behavior. `python -m pytest -q`: 6 passed. This local fix has not been pushed or deployed.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
